10,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,785,47311,400,79,2075,15087,67901,400,79,7,16,8,284,220,17,16,15,3,323,198,59,9697,87,488,220,16,15,8,281,7,17,87,8,284,220,23,2075,481,220,19,8,281,2075,488,220,21,10699,60,1958,678,1931,5109,400,87,2418,220,7379,400,79,7,16,15,568,3,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nThe polynomial $p(x)$ satisfies $p(1) = 210$ and\n\\[(x + 10) p(2x) = 8(x - 4) p(x + 6)\\]for all real numbers $x.$  Find $p(10).$","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"662d156f48ca7b07de17476e2f9ad4da082b76e5839bea23146cb98f6a33c1ee"},"seconds":67.95044231414795,"seed":994056254616445156,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem, we first need to analyze the given functional equation:\n\\[\n(x + 10) p(2x) = 8(x - 4) p(x + 6).\n\\]\nWe will substitute specific values of \\(x\\) to find more information about \\(p(x)\\).\n\nFirst, let's substitute \\(x = -10\\):\n\\[\n(-10 + 10) p(2(-10)) = 8(-10 - 4) p(-10 + 6) \\implies 0 = -112 p(-4) \\implies p(-4) = 0.\n\\]\nThis tells us that \\(x = -4\\) is a root of \\(p(x)\\).\n\nNext, let's substitute \\(x = 4\\):\n\\[\n(4 + 10) p(2 \\cdot 4) = 8(4 - 4) p(4 + 6) \\implies 14 p(8) = 0 \\implies p(8) = 0.\n\\]\nThis tells us that \\(x = 8\\) is also a root of \\(p(x)\\).\n\nNow we know that \\(p(x)\\) has at least the roots \\(x = -4\\) and \\(x = 8\\). Let's assume \\(p(x)\\) can be written as:\n\\[\np(x) = c (x + 4)(x - 8) q(x),\n\\]\nwhere \\(c\\) is a constant and \\(q(x)\\) is some polynomial. We need to determine the form of \\(q(x)\\). To do this, we substitute \\(p(x) = c (x + 4)(x - 8) q(x)\\) into the original functional equation.\n\nFirst, calculate \\(p(2x)\\):\n\\[\np(2x) = c (2x + 4)(2x - 8) q(2x) = 4c (x + 2)(x - 4) q(2x).\n\\]\nThen, substitute into the left side of the functional equation:\n\\[\n(x + 10) p(2x) = (x + 10) \\cdot 4c (x + 2)(x - 4) q(2x) = 4c (x + 10)(x + 2)(x - 4) q(2x).\n\\]\nNext, calculate \\(p(x + 6)\\):\n\\[\np(x + 6) = c ((x + 6) + 4)((x + 6) - 8) q(x + 6) = c (x + 10)(x - 2) q(x + 6).\n\\]\nThen, substitute into the right side of the functional equation:\n\\[\n8(x - 4) p(x + 6) = 8(x - 4) \\cdot c (x + 10)(x - 2) q(x + 6) = 8c (x - 4)(x + 10)(x - 2) q(x + 6).\n\\]\nEquating the two sides, we get:\n\\[\n4c (x + 10)(x + 2)(x - 4) q(2x) = 8c (x - 4)(x + 10)(x - 2) q(x + 6).\n\\]\nCanceling out the common factors \\(4c (x + 10)(x - 4)\\) from both sides, we get:\n\\[\n(x + 2) q(2x) = 2(x - 2) q(x + 6).\n\\]\nTo satisfy this equation for all \\(x\\), \\(q(x)\\) must be a constant polynomial. Let \\(q(x) = k\\), then:\n\\[\n(x + 2) k = 2(x - 2) k \\implies x + 2 = 2x - 4 \\implies x = 6.\n\\]\nThis is a contradiction unless \\(k = 0\\), but since \\(p(x)\\) is not identically zero, we conclude \\(q(x) = 1\\). Therefore, \\(p(x) = c(x + 4)(x - 8)\\).\n\nWe are given \\(p(1) = 210\\):\n\\[\np(1) = c(1 + 4)(1 - 8) = c \\cdot 5 \\cdot (-7) = -35c = 210 \\implies c = -6.\n\\]\nThus, the polynomial is:\n\\[\np(x) = -6(x + 4)(x - 8).\n\\]\nFinally, we need to find \\(p(10)\\):\n\\[\np(10) = -6(10 + 4)(10 - 8) = -6 \\cdot 14 \\cdot 2 = -168.\n\\]\nThe answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-168}.\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{-168}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
